# Secrets, and nothing else. This file is the first of #32's three guards: it stops a "git add ."
# from staging a secret, the ".githooks/pre-commit" hook refuses the commit when one is staged
# anyway, and the "Secret scan" workflow reports it after the fact on the pull request.
#
# ! None of the three blocks anything on GitHub's side: no ruleset is imported, so no CI check is
# required before a merge. The local hook is therefore the only one
# of the three that really refuses anything -- and "git commit --no-verify" bypasses it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment files
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Artificial Intelligence stack uses NO ".env" file: the role of #31 interpolates the values directly into the rendered
# "docker-compose", written 0600 on the managed node and never versioned.
# The patterns below are useful all the same: they cover the ".env" a human creates to start a
# container by hand while debugging, which is exactly the file nobody thinks of deleting before
# committing.
#
# ! The order is load-bearing: moving a "!" line above the pattern it cancels neutralises it.
*.env
.env
.env.*
# ... except the example, should one ever appear.
!.env.example
!*.env.example
# ... and except a Jinja template that would RENDER an environment file: without this line,
# ".env.*" swallows "templates/.env.j2" and "git status" does not even show it
# (measured: "git check-ignore -v" -> ".gitignore:.env.*").
!.env*.j2

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Keys, certificates, passwords
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.key
*.pem
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
# The Ansible vault password, never the vault itself: an encrypted vault is MADE to be versioned.
# Do not widen this pattern to "vault*", which would exclude the very content we want to track.
.vault_pass

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Service data and local artefacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# "storage/" is Qdrant's default persistence directory (#3): a test started by hand from the
# repository root creates it here.
storage/
.ansible/
*.retry
__pycache__/
.venv/
